WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.267
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.890
RON JOLLY: Journalism
today, I believe, just

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:07.970
about everybody reporting the
news has some kind of agenda.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:11.210
They're starting off
point is not ground zero,

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.060
it's from where they are
on the left or the right.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.690
And it's very confusing or very
difficult for news consumers

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.030
to find anything to trust.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.600
So it's crucial that we
really examine what journalism

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.680
is and should be and teach
people proper journalism,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.090
because it's the conduit.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.110
It's what we all need.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:31.730
It's what ties us
together and how

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.390
we communicate and understand
what's going on in our city,

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.400
our town, our world.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.670
I have throughout much of
my career on talk radio

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.145
interviewed professors,
people from Hillsdale.

00:00:43.145 --> 00:00:45.020
And I said during the
interview, why don't we

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.990
have more Hillsdale
Colleges in this country?

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:51.470
And I got a letter a couple
of weeks later and they said,

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.830
we really agree with you.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.470
So we're going to start a
scholarship in your name

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:58.730
for Hillsdale College.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:00.500
I just-- I was beside myself.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.490
I couldn't believe it.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.400
The scholarship will be used
for a bright, ambitious student

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.390
from Michigan who is interested
in journalism and radio.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:11.600
The journalism program
at Hillsdale College

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.700
has produced great
success stories.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.160
We have former students
of Hillsdale now working

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.800
at The Wall Street
Journal, The Detroit News,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.230
and many other publications.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.960
The radio and journalism
program at Hillsdale,

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.870
Radio Free Hillsdale,
has won numerous awards.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.450
And they've just been named
the best college radio station

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:30.230
in Michigan.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.600
Hillsdale College has a
great journalism program

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:36.300
because the students there,
like all Hillsdale students,

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.690
they learn about
foundational things

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:41.030
they should know,
like our constitution,

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.850
why do we have freedom in this
country, what's it all about.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.670
And it gives them context
to report on everything.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.330
So you match a classical
education with journalism,

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.390
and you're going to produce
responsible, trustworthy,

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:55.980
knowledgeable journalists
in the future.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.840
This is a matching scholarship.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.560
And that means anybody
who supports Hillsdale

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.930
for the education
that they provide,

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.540
you can donate any amount
and it will be doubled.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.289
So you can donate $10 and
you'll make an impact, and that

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:13.940
will be doubled, $20, $100,
any amount, $1,000, $10,000,

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.610
you name it, please give
to the Ron Jolly Challenge

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.590
at Hillsdale College
before our deadline.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:22.270
And remember, whatever
you give will be doubled.

